ave plans to assassinate  bella real the mayor-elect of gotham  this leads to a big finale and alongside  selena carl batman manages to put an end  to them however it's very bittersweet  and as we mentioned earlier this will  likely set up a no man's land situation  where the entire city is abandoned by  the government and left to fend for  itself though this was slightly touched  upon in the dark knight rises here they  can really rip things open and have an  all-out war where the criminals and  supervillains buy for power zero yeah  also had the streets of gotham transform  into a savage wasteland which had the  riddler at the helm throughout both  batman pretty much dropped the bruce  wayne playboy persona which robert  pattinson's version hasn't developed yet  so i think they would make sense to be  the next storylines i think that he will  adopt it eventually but in the likes of  both earth one and zero yeah it was  alfred that convinced him that he needed  a face he could show to the people bruce  wayne has connections that batman  doesn't and he's gonna need every  possible avenue he has at his disposal  to stop the joker if he does end up  working with the riddler they have a lot  of interesting ways that they can take  things and i'm very curious to see where  they go next with it now as for selena  she very much says that the city is  beyond saving and decides to leave a  bloodhaven bloodhaven is actually a  neighboring city to gotham that the  likes of nightwing ended up being a  defender of rare rumors that zoe kravitz  will be getting her own hbo max show too  and with the way that the movie leaves  things off i definitely think there's a  strong possibility of it we could also  have the gcpd show basically showing  from the police point of view what's  going to happen with those in the city  now that major areas of it are flooded  it has been confirmed that the penguin  show is closer to shooting but that  could end up being more of a book of  boba fett type series where we get a lot  of flashbacks which hey can't wait to go  back to that hey maybe they'll put him  in a nice pool or something and i  thought my jokes were bad  now as with my thoughts on the movie i  have to say i was completely blown away  by it and not only did it meet my  expectations but it surpassed them in  every single way a lot of the chatter  around this movie will be is it better  than the dark knight which still to this  day remains as the benchmark for dc  movies i think having just come out of  it that i'm gonna have a lot of recency  bias because i've just seen it and when  you're this hyped you can be like best  movie ever made best movie of all time  so i don't want to let that cloud my  judgment i'm going to let it marinate  for a bit but my initial thoughts are  that the dark knight works better as a  movie for general audiences because it's  got a lot of great action scenes some  good humor and you know it's just sort  of a blockbuster movie now whilst this  has those elements too it feels like a  film rather than simply being a popcorn  flick reeves has worn his influences on  his sleeves when talking about this and  even niche films like conversation get a  nod with the opening scenes being very  similar to that movie i don't know which  of the two are preferred but yet that  should let you know how highly i think  of the batman this is absolutely  brilliant and for me it takes a lot of  the boxes in terms of telling a story  that's not only faithful to the comics  but also unique in what it does for this  version batman is someone who's such a  flexible character and one year you can  do batman v superman and the next the  lego batman movie without it feeling  like either or untrue to who he is  greaves has done an incredible job of  putting his own stamp on the character  and along with this is the phenomenal  cast there's pattinson who bats it out  of the park zoe kravitz who might be the  best selena kyle ever colin farrell in  an unrecognizable transformation and  jeffrey wright who brings the gritty and  granite betrayal that you'd expect  everyone does an incredible job and  though i have nitpicks over the film  including its narration heavy third act  i feel they did a phenomenal job  especially for a first attempt this  movie has me so hyped for what's to come  and i really hope that dc learn lessons  from this in joker and decide to  greenlight more directly driven takes on  characters that aren't crippled by  continuity outstanding job and i think  that this movie is a masterpiece where  we go next i don't know but for this  film i'm gonna give it a 10 out of 10.  you  are justice  [Music]  please do not lie  what is the price for your  blind bag  [Music]  obviously i'd love to hear your thoughts  on the movie if you agree and if you  enjoyed the video then don't forget to  subscribe right now we have a breakdown  discussing why we love the dark knight  so much and i'd love to see you over  there right after this if not then  thanks for singing until the end of the  video really appreciate it and i hope to  see on the next one take care peace
 

